From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Host the controller's drivers without nsiproxy on request.

Patch 1003 hosts nsiproxy in every 64-bit PS5 game, after the
controller's HID drivers when WINE_NTOSKRNL_HOSTED is 1. A game that
breaks with nsiproxy had no way to keep the HID drivers without it.

The value winebus now means the controller's HID drivers alone: the pad
waits for its drivers as with 1, and nsiproxy is not loaded. The values
1 and nsiproxy keep their meaning, so a launcher that never sets winebus
sees no change.
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -4447,8 +4447,9 @@
  * set, ntoskrnl runs drivers on threads of this process, started before the
  * game's entry point: with the value 1, the controller's HID drivers
  * (winebus and the ones it loads), so that the game finds the controller
- * when it first looks, then nsiproxy; with any other value nsiproxy only.
- * iphlpapi reads the network interfaces from nsiproxy's \\.\Nsi device.
+ * when it first looks, then nsiproxy; with the value winebus, those drivers
+ * alone, for a game that must not get nsiproxy; with any other value nsiproxy
+ * only. iphlpapi reads the network interfaces from nsiproxy's \\.\Nsi device.
  * nsiproxy's Unix side has no WoW64 thunks, so a 32-bit game gets the
  * controller's drivers only. */
 static void start_hosted_drivers(void)
@@ -4461,7 +4462,7 @@
     NTSTATUS (CDECL *host_load)( const WCHAR *driver );
     UNICODE_STRING value;
     WCHAR buffer[16];
-    BOOL pad, nsi;
+    BOOL pad, nsi, winebus;
     HMODULE module;
     NTSTATUS status;
 
@@ -4475,9 +4476,10 @@
     /* Only the game: Wine's own programs (explorer, services) inherit the variable too. */
     if (image->Buffer && (!wcsnicmp( image->Buffer, system_dir, wcslen(system_dir) ) ||
                           !wcsnicmp( image->Buffer, L"C:\\windows\\syswow64\\", 20 ))) return;
-    pad = !status && value.Length == sizeof(WCHAR) && buffer[0] == '1';
+    winebus = !status && value.Length == 7 * sizeof(WCHAR) && !wcsncmp( buffer, L"winebus", 7 );
+    pad = winebus || (!status && value.Length == sizeof(WCHAR) && buffer[0] == '1');
 #ifdef _WIN64
-    nsi = !NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset;
+    nsi = !winebus && !NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset;
 #else
     nsi = FALSE;
 #endif
